cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark, its targets, or its judge-validation recipe, please cite it."
title: "Roast Anything: a roast-generation benchmark with specificity and truth gates and a damage-test-validated LLM judge"
authors:
  - family-names: Chen
    given-names: Yuanrui
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-12
url: "https://github.com/yuanrui3/AI-benchmark-for-roasting"
repository-code: "https://github.com/yuanrui3/AI-benchmark-for-roasting"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - LLM humor benchmark
  - roast generation
  - computational humor
  - LLM-as-a-judge
  - humor evaluation
  - Chinese humor
  - comedy writing evaluation
  - Bradley-Terry leaderboard
abstract: >-
  A bilingual (English and Chinese) benchmark for roast generation. A roast counts only if it passes a specificity
  test against a near-twin and a truth check against a verified fact sheet; taste is then scored by blind pairwise
  comparison. The LLM judge is validated without human raters by seven damage tests and anchored to public
  crowd-preference data from the New Yorker caption contest and SemEval-2020 FunLines. Results order Claude Opus 5.5
  above Sonnet 5.5 above Haiku 5.5 and show that a house-style comedy skill beats plain and fact-fed prompting.
